One way to output a newline is to output std::endl (which stands for “end line”):#include <iostream> // for std::cout and std::endl
int main()
{
 std::cout << "Hi!" << std::endl; // std::endl will cause the cursor to move to the next line
 std::cout << "My name is Alex." << std::endl;
 return 0;
}
This prints:Hi!
My name is Alex.
